{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Classify beverages at or below 0.5% ABV as alcohol free",
        "additional_details": "For context: a ripe banana or a bread roll can hold as much alcohol as a 0.5% beer, yet the beer can\u2019t call itself alcohol-free. We are concerned that the world\u2019s strictest 0.05% limit is easy for big brands with big budgets to hit and market, but a costly barrier for small independent brewers. It also fuels the myth that a 0.5% beer is much like a real pint, when the amount is negligible. We think that aligning with the 0.5% international standard would mean honest, consistent labelling people can actually trust.",
        "background": "Change the law so any drink at 0.5% ABV or below can be labelled \u201calcohol-free\u201d. At 0.05%, the UK\u2019s limit is the strictest in the world. The Government has consulted twice and committed to it. Stop consulting and act.",
